=== where do the curves cross? ===
  on_400 overtakes off_150 at B = 97 oracle-s (0.03 core-hours for the whole 60-target benchmark)
    below that, off_150 is better; above it the gap grows to 10 targets
  on_400 overtakes off_400 at B = 70 oracle-s (0.02 core-hours for the whole 60-target benchmark)
    below that, off_400 is better; above it the gap grows to 10 targets

=== scheduler slack: how far is 'one trajectory per target' from optimal? ===
  system      B of the flat policy   flat S   optimal S at same B   slack
  off_150                     2985     3.25                 10.39    3.20x
  on_400                      6714     5.50                 17.42    3.17x
  this is the quantity the trajectory experiment moved: it did not raise S_inf (12 -> 10 distinct
  targets) but it closed part of this gap. Capability and scheduling are separate coordinates.

=== a known bias, stated: S_inf from 8 seeds is a LOWER bound ===
  a target with true p = 0.05 shows 0 wins in 8 seeds with probability 0.66
  a target with true p = 0.10 shows 0 wins in 8 seeds with probability 0.43
  a target with true p = 0.20 shows 0 wins in 8 seeds with probability 0.17
  so S_inf is underestimated, and the two coordinates have OPPOSITE sampling needs:
    measuring S_inf  -> many seeds, few targets
    measuring B_half -> few seeds, many targets
  a single sweep cannot estimate both well; the eval suite should budget for each separately.

